    "problem_statement_fixed": "A log append callback must run once for each append while registered, receive the log and new index, and stop running after it is cleared.\n\nThe callback is registered with a log by calling log_set_append_cb(struct log *log, cb), where cb is a pointer to a callback function with the signature void (struct log *log, uint32_t idx), or NULL to clear the callback. The callback must be invoked with the log that was appended to and the index of the newly appended log entry, and it must not be invoked when no callback is registered."
